  "Question": "An arithmetic sequence has \\(a_1=2\\) and \\(d=3\\). What is the sum of the first 5 terms?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "40",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(S_5=5\\times2+5\\times4\\times3/2=10+30=40\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: List and add the terms\n\nStarting at \\(2\\), add \\(3\\) to obtain each next term. The first five terms are \\(2,5,8,11,14\\), so their sum is\n\\[\n2+5+8+11+14=40.\n\\]\nThus the sum is \\(40\\).",
